1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:45,640
He was an awful person. He had this story about the time in his life when he was someone important. He'd brag about it all the time. I remember it well because he made me listen to it every time. Every single time.

3
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:29,980
His insights had been expelled. But deep inside the cabin, there was an individual who still actually looked like a person. But he... He was not in any condition to talk.

4
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:36,300
The hell's this? Is it valuable or something?

5
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:58,800
That... That compass stands. It's there, the place where the compass stands straight up. It's there. A giant pit. A terrifying, wretched abyss that reaches to the bottom of the world.

6
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:13,540
I couldn't bear to look. I just couldn't. It's really there. The Golden City's there. It's true. It's inside the giant... The giant man-eating pit.

7
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:31,760
That's what the guy said. Then the old man just died on us. Anyway, pretty nice, right? And remember, you are nothing like me. Got it? Hold still.

8
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:52,380
I'm not like him with that boastful story he clung to. I prepared myself for that one purpose. For that one single thing.

9
00:02:52,380 --> 00:03:05,260
No. No. No. I just knew I longed for it. A place. A place where no one knew me.

10
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:21,900
You know about the Golden City, right? They say it turns things to gold. Maybe even a worthless little thing like this. Or even a dirty, used-up girl. You think if I bring you two to the city, I can get rich?

11
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:28,080
I longed for a place where his voice, which still echoes even though he's gone, would finally vanish.

12
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:47,580
The journey is rough. No matter how much I trained, I'll never get used to being seasick.

13
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:57,600
It has already been 20 days since the last port of call. The fish we sometimes catch, and the booze that hasn't gone bad, are purely treats to us now.

14
00:03:57,600 --> 00:04:09,240
Our leader, Razukyan, is once again eating raw bugs. He catches them down in the hold. He says it prevents disease.

15
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:16,840
Then there's the horizon. It constantly disappears. Only to show itself moments later.

16
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:20,300
Over and over again.

17
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:24,300
The only thing I have is plenty of nausea.

18
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,300
That's great.

19
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,960
It's not great at all.

20
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:30,400
Getting used to vomiting.

21
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:33,300
But the precious food...

22
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:38,240
Don't worry about it. We still have another month's supply of hardtack.

23
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,660
Besides, we're almost there.

24
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:44,100
To the spot where the star compass stands up straight.

25
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:48,500
And these uncharted seas and rough winds, it's the only thing we can trust.

26
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,200
But, uh...

27
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:53,160
Are you sure that it's alright for me to hold on to it?

28
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:54,860
Of course it is.

29
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:58,460
You're one of the revered three sages of Ganja now.

30
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:03,400
Besides, you're the one who brought me that compass in the first place.

31
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:05,660
Like it was some sort of destiny, you know?

32
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:10,400
Seriously, though, you're our guidepost on this journey before us.

33
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:13,360
Don't you worry.

34
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:16,440
My gut is always right.

35
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:17,960
We're almost there.

36
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:19,320
So, cheer up.

37
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,920
Anyway, I'm gonna go catch me some rats.

38
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,180
Don't mind him.

39
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:32,800
Belaf.

40
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:35,400
It's not that he's insincere.

41
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:37,020
I think you know that by now.

42
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:41,220
But sometimes he, and I guess that goes for the rest of us too,

43
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:44,060
just can't seem to put into words the truth he senses.

44
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,560
And that's why he can come off like that.

45
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:50,200
We didn't take him seriously at first because we thought it was all in his head.

46
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:51,800
But he's real.

47
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:53,740
Like he's touched by the divine.

48
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:59,540
In his case, even if the Golden City doesn't exist, he'll probably find it anyway.

49
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:04,680
Not to mention, he foretold that you'd join our group and become one of the three sages.

50
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:07,180
And that was the day right before you appeared.

51
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:09,860
Such is the power of his magnificent gift.

52
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:16,580
Yeah, but, Belaf, is it really okay for me to be one of the sages?

53
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:20,500
It's just that I don't have any sort of gifts like that.

54
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:23,580
What do you want me for?

55
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:27,480
I'm not worth trying to sell with this ugly body of mine.

56
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:30,340
The only thing I can do is take care of others.

57
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:35,140
Just what exactly do you think beauty is?

58
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:37,020
I don't know.

59
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:40,880
Oh, uh, is it something like you, Belaf?

60
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:41,880
Full of confidence?

61
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,300
That sort of thing?

62
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,080
I just don't know.

63
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:49,920
It is not beauty.

64
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,680
Just because it is beautiful.

65
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:53,320
It is not ugly.

66
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,340
Just because it is ugly.

67
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:58,320
Your...

68
00:06:58,320 --> 00:06:59,940
Eyes sure are pretty.

69
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:01,220
There you go.

70
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,080
Beauty is in the eyes.

71
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:04,560
Understand?

72
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,780
Not the eyes in a physical sense.

73
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:08,920
Take it to mean...

74
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:09,820
The look they have.

75
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:14,780
Position, status, prestige, appearance...

76
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:17,660
And even confidence are not the true nature of beauty.

77
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:20,160
Even if your wounds fester,

78
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,560
Or you topple over in the face of injustice.

79
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:25,480
Even if you are forced down when you try to stand.

80
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,280
To continue.

81
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:29,340
To glare with affection and longing.

82
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:32,720
That look in the eyes is the true nature of beauty.

83
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,220
You have eyes full of darkness.

84
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:39,120
Affix your eyes upon that darkness.

85
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:43,120
For the light that no one else has found can only exist in the true void.

86
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:48,300
And remember, you are more capable and lovely than you can imagine.

87
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,500
Very much so.

88
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:54,920
So no matter how dirty or unsightly, my eyes will not be deceived.

89
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:57,180
Keep that in mind and trust yourself.

90
00:07:57,180 --> 00:08:03,680
Wicco, we need you to come inside.

91
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:05,640
Sumasura has a fever.

92
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:08,560
Okay, I'll be right there.

93
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:13,340
Uplifting as always.

94
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:15,180
Did you call her dirty?

95
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:16,320
No, whatever.

96
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:19,340
You know I was just trying to take a deeper look into things.

97
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:29,300
How are the others doing?

98
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,800
Jomi's and R's are the only ones still afloat.

99
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:35,000
Wazukyan, look!

100
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,020
That cargo's from Jomi's hold.

101
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:40,740
I fear that means they're gone.

102
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,540
Hey, Bella, Wazukyan!

103
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:44,680
Look at the compass!

104
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,240
Huh?

105
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:54,520
What is that?

106
00:08:54,520 --> 00:09:08,260
Land in an impassable patch of sea.

107
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:09,500
It's gotta be!

108
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:15,780
I wanna know where the people are

109
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:22,360
I take my dreams to life

110
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:26,900
Okay, who wants to be the first ashore?

111
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:31,560
All right, we are finally here

112
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:33,580
Where our new lives begin

113
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:35,820
Let it echo far and wide

114
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:38,160
To the people of our abandoned homeland

115
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:41,620
Yours are the feet that will crush injustice

116
00:09:41,620 --> 00:10:06,200
It's really here

117
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,000
Yes, it is

118
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,480
To the one

119
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:14,420
And I know where I belong

120
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:21,700
Go to guard

121
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:23,560
Who will the place

122
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:24,320
Because if you have a forever

123
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:24,980
But you will use your house

124
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:25,720
Let as of your behalf

125
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:27,520
Who will play

126
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:28,400
Like my hai

127
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,540
What is that such?

128
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:30,640
Now that we are of course

129
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:31,160
Look at me

130
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,140
From Gerson

131
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:32,600
How does Gerson

132
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,400
How does Gerson

133
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,040
Go to Gerson

134
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:36,700
How

135
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:36,960
Do.....

136
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:38,200
Soc

137
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:38,600
He's saying

138
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,220
He's saying

139
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:47,340
Um, Mozu-hyon, these people were not mentioned in our intel.

140
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:48,620
Ha ha ha!

141
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:51,520
What the?

142
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:55,540
Ah, yeah. This is the real thrill of an adventure.

143
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:26,120
Ah, what strange cliffs. Is this here the giant pit?

144
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:30,320
How's it going?

145
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:35,500
It would seem those who came before us were violent and domineering, so they're reluctant to share information.

146
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:39,000
Ah, haji! Haji!

147
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:44,600
What is it? What's that guy saying and why is he pointing at me?

148
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:46,000
Kephu, kefu!

149
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:47,180
Precious, you say?

150
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:48,960
Kephu, risore!

151
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:50,680
He says it's a precious thing.

152
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:52,180
Korusomu!

153
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:53,900
Essential part?

154
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,900
Hajime korusomu, Guko.

155
00:12:01,140 --> 00:12:05,120
It looks like he's telling us that he's willing to help us out in exchange for the compass.

156
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:15,080
Here you go.

157
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:22,360
Are you sure about this?

158
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:25,060
I mean, you've had your gaze on it for so long.

159
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,140
It's what guides you.

160
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,640
It's fine, really.

161
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:31,560
The object of my gaze lies within the darkness.

162
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:37,380
Uh, Borlaff, I... I want to... I need to go looking for it.

163
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:41,420
That light that no one else has found yet.

164
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:49,340
It's so big.

165
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:52,680
Can there really be people living in a place like this?

166
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:55,500
That's insane.

167
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:57,500
The Golden City.

168
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,840
The natives have told me that they call this place Shoro.

169
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,360
And that means?

170
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:04,160
The capital of the unreturned.

171
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:08,220
They also said you'll never be able to come back, but that the city does exist.

172
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,620
What's going on?

173
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:22,360
Um, well, this little kid, it seems that she followed us all the way here.

174
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:27,980
Uh, wha? Why is she sniffing me?

175
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,580
Excuse me a moment.

176
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:30,420
Uh, wha?

177
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:30,740
Ah!

178
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:32,560
This tattoo.

179
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:35,800
These wounds are still fresh.

180
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:39,100
An infant.

181
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:40,460
Impossible.

182
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:44,780
As she cannot bear children, she is hereby exiled to the Giant Pit.

183
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:46,360
That's roughly what it says.

184
00:13:46,540 --> 00:13:48,360
That sounds so horrible.

185
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:58,960
We don't have spare resources to keep her safe.

186
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:01,380
Yeah, well, she's from here, though.

187
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:03,440
She might know a lot about the pit.

188
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:04,460
Besides them.

189
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:05,580
Not only that.

190
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,580
Just look at her, you guys.

191
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:08,980
She's kind of adorable.

192
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,700
What's your call, Wazukyan?

193
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:12,880
Hmm.

194
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:16,560
Well, we're in terrible need of a guide.

195
00:14:16,820 --> 00:14:18,200
One less thing to worry about.

196
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:35,800
Can't really see down into the pit too well from here, I'm afraid.

197
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:36,660
One second.

198
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:37,600
I'll climb up.

199
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:42,620
What is it?

200
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:54,320
What the hell?

201
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:58,160
What's this?

202
00:14:58,540 --> 00:14:59,120
Poison?

203
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:02,040
Mayazuma, Kurohomachi.

204
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,900
Mayazuma, Zomu.

205
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:04,620
Sorry.

206
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,760
I don't understand what you're saying.

207
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:13,980
She's saying, if you ascend within the interior, you will be eaten.

208
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:15,260
Hmm?

209
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:16,540
By what?

210
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:17,840
Zomu.

211
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:21,100
The closest translation would be, the curse.

212
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:26,260
See?

213
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:29,320
We really do need a guide, don't we?

214
00:15:30,460 --> 00:15:31,820
I'm counting on you.

215
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:34,200
Now let's go, shall we?

216
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,200
To the city!

217
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:39,900
It's not like I was feeling triumphant or anything.

218
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:43,340
But my pulse was racing like it never had before.

219
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:50,660
We were Gonja, a group of outcasts that set out for the Golden City.

220
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:53,500
We had been forsaken by our homelands.

221
00:15:55,060 --> 00:16:00,940
Believing in a nameless god, we roamed searching for its source, and in those who were no longer human.

222
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:09,680
We found paranormal relics, otherworldly scenery, and the curse.

223
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:13,520
Everything had all the mystery we'd been hoping for.

224
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,900
All the intensity we had been searching for.

225
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:24,540
So surely, the source of all this wonder, must be here too.

226
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:28,520
Whoa.

227
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:39,020
Hey!

228
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:40,660
B worked!

229
00:16:40,660 --> 00:16:41,960
Wow!

230
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,200
I can see outside!

231
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:47,180
Bigger than I thought and it's so quiet too hard to believe we're in a whirlpool

232
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:54,700
This smell though, I recognize it there must be some eternal fortune incense in here

233
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:59,440
Maybe so cave raiders burn it for celebrations and even funerals sometimes

234
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:05,480
It smells like someone is burning it fresh

235
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:11,840
I bet that bastard Bondrood lights them every once in a while. Yeah Bondrood. What was that guy after down here?

236
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:17,040
Anyway, who knows doesn't seem like it's simply reaching the bottom of the netherworld though

237
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:20,160
He said something about the next two thousand years

238
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:26,080
Well, I sure don't feel like going back and asking him everything. He says is laced with poison

239
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:29,120
No doubt anything. He'd tell us would be self-serving

240
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:34,240
Yeah, let's focus on what's next instead. We've had enough of that creep

241
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:40,720
Honestly, I just want to be genuinely happy about continuing on with you guys down to the bottom of the netherworld

242
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:43,840
No, no, no gee

243
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:50,960
Nah, it is annoying that he can still peek in on my vision, but I guess the good news is that's all he can really do to us now

244
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:55,280
So then let's show him our big grand adventure

245
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,880
I'm glad to see you thinking positively

246
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:02,720
You purposefully snuck up on me didn't you rag?

247
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:04,720
Don't sniff me

248
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:08,320
How'd he do that? I didn't even hear him coming

249
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:14,400
It's it's moving

250
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,360
It's going down

251
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,800
Um, I just rubbed Prushka a bit and I think I felt something

252
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:22,800
Uh, uh

253
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:27,040
Adventures have a strange way of suddenly getting started, you know

254
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:30,480
Riko, don't mess around with the Prushka stone

255
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:33,280
Wouldn't be very funny if we started going up instead

256
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,080
Yeah, sorry

